# Named full vibrational Raman of LiH: the named twin of
# src/examples/qc/response_lih_raman_full (same molecule, rung and settings).
# One rung (protocol 1e-4, k 6): the static polarizability tensor and the
# complete polarizability gradient over all 3N = 6 nuclear coordinates
# (raman.atoms and raman.directions omitted: every atom, every axis), so the
# engine builds the Hessian from the same six nuclear response states and
# passes its normal-mode analysis through (one mode, its Raman activity and
# depolarization ratio). Legs: 3 dipole + 6 nuclear-displacement; 18 quadratic
# sources. The numbers are a regression baseline at k 6, not converged Raman
# values (see the twin's header).
# Run: madqc named_lih_raman.in --prefix=LiH-raman
molecule LiH
  units angstrom
  eprec 1e-6
  no_orient true
  Li 0.0 0.0 -0.803105264950
  H  0.0 0.0  0.803105264950
end

moldft gs
  molecule LiH
  xc hf
  L 50
  localize new
  protocol [1e-4]
  dconv 1e-4
  maxiter 30
  requested_properties [energy, dipole]
end

molresponse raman
  reference gs
  protocol [1e-4]
  dconv 1e-4
  maxiter 60
  kain true
  print_level 1
  requested_properties [polarizability, raman]
  polarizability.frequencies [0.0]
  polarizability.frequency_units au
  polarizability.components [xx, yy, zz]
  raman.frequencies [0.0]
  raman.frequency_units au
  raman.components [xx, yy, zz, xy, xz, yz]
end
